    "body": "Quoted from @eatstorming on https://github.com/brave/browser-ios/issues/266\r\n\r\n> My personal reasoning for this is just annoyance; the main page of an app I use for extended periods of time, changing based on what I've been browsing, annoys me.\r\n>\r\n>However, there is also a privacy issue at play: an eavesdropper can see what you've been browsing if they manage to look at your screen when you open a new tab.\r\n>\r\n>I understand that for a lot of people this may be a wanted feature. I just don't see why it can't be toggled on and off. So, please, add such an option to this otherwise awesome app.\r\n\r\n\r\nFollowing _at least_ Brave desktop's options (https://github.com/brave/browser-ios/issues/266#issuecomment-276412996) would be good.\r\n\r\nSimilar to search engines, it would probably be to make this configurable for normal and private mode individually. As pointed out, this can be a potential privacy issues, and some people may not want top sites showing in a specific mode.",
